d up weapons launches in recent weeks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Japanese journalist arrest in Russia's Far East draws rebuke from Tokyo in latest diplomatic spat with Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb67caf37ac5123844b0e345b9db1544dd4d2a9f3a66e4e8e281c44e4236a87b</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T17:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japanese-journalist-arrest-in-russia-s-far-east-draws-rebuke-from-tokyo-in-latest-diplomatic-spat-wi/a-79663428--29b99abb7ad1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japanese-journalist-arrest-in-russia-s-far-east-draws-rebuke-from-tokyo-in-latest-diplomatic-spat-with-moscow/a-79663428?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A journalist for a Japanese newspaper was arrested on suspicion of spying in Russia's Far East. A geopolitical rivalry over disputed islands in the region has recently caused tension.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesian VIP prison scandal exposes inequality across Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d59aa5087f04db02482f1afd14c882597454287fdf6bbe66a431fea608fdf25</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T14:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesian-vip-prison-scandal-exposes-inequality-across-southeast-asia/a-79659535--b1904f02177b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesian-vip-prison-scandal-exposes-inequality-across-southeast-asia/a-79659535?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Luxury accommodation uncovered at an Indonesian prison has reignited concerns about preferential treatment for wealthy convicts across Southeast Asia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China's influence in the gaming industry is growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:850fa26cad0f5afffbfc1309f2f972a2ae8b827d8cd8c9d509e6921c4b91f736</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T11:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755--447380e7608a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Home to more than 700 million gamers, China is the world's largest gaming market — but it's also one of the most tightly regulated. The effects reach far beyond China, impacting players around the world.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>India news: 'Cockroach' leaders sent to judicial custody amid protest crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79385ec7fc8faf231da804139a285a2f969d5c48b03131bc67eecd83c3e44556</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T05:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-cockroach-leaders-sent-to-judicial-custody-amid-protest-crackdown/live-79656344--74c790a24516.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-cockroach-leaders-sent-to-judicial-custody-amid-protest-crackdown/live-79656344?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three of India's Cockroach movement leaders will spend five days in jail over charges of trespassing into what was until recently a designated protest site. In other news, Marco Rubio is set to visit India.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How will emergency rule in Pakistan's northwest affect Afghan ties?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9515348318085a9faf69aecc2b0eeeb06c3dd09bb9b82dc548d80bfd4b43f0cf</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T16:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-will-emergency-rule-in-pakistan-s-northwest-affect-afghan-ties/a-79654262--94171911b4d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-will-emergency-rule-in-pakistan-s-northwest-affect-afghan-ties/a-79654262?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pakistan's decision to suspend Khyber Pakhtunkhwa's provincial government could further strain already tense relations between Islamabad and Kabul.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India: Can 'cockroaches' threaten Modi's political grip?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bf31631c10a7b4b2abc35ffdb32b909e0d1eb7aa42b9a7ce604828bf48f0e5f</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-can-cockroaches-threaten-modi-s-political-grip/a-79649732--1196fbece1f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-can-cockroaches-threaten-modi-s-political-grip/a-79649732?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Thousands detained, leaders arrested on arrival, and a capital under lockdown: The youth-led protests against the election chief have the attention of the Indian government. But experts say toppling it is another matter.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India opposition huddle over tea after thousands march in their Delhi protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e555b1c57e5970d6add61541ea17780345fd3ff93e324073e13cb584dfea2694</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T06:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-opposition-huddle-over-tea-after-thousands-march-in-their-delhi-protest/live-79646819--4d3738030bbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-opposition-huddle-over-tea-after-thousands-march-in-their-delhi-protest/live-79646819?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Congress' Rahul Gandhi hosted oppositon MPs for tea after rallying thousands in Monday's election protest. The 'Cockroach' movement says its leaders have been detained during a flash protest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India faces water and power shortages after weak monsoon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f547f8791b1d1018463d56a90efd9b4239bf38826a14bbfb242f057f211f28dc</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540--3ab74afcb33c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A weak monsoon in India is hitting farmers, water supplies and the power system, while raising wider questions about increasingly erratic rainfall and the economic costs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea warns of AI-aided hacking after bank data breaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec0425816692f33c7a0a7519e05a1b190bae9f131963cc8a7093a63f608bc804</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922--3290ee11faa1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seoul is alarmed after a recent breach of South Korean banks' cyber defenses that reportedly involved AI-assisted hacking. Officials warn such methods could be used to also target other sectors and government agencies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A brutal assault reignites fears over women's safety in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe7f6cb5bce7aa02fc3277cd12dcece65f8de19777b343b0a9a88a31a7bc8a45</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T17:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471--bceecddefb45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A string of sexual violence cases has revived questions about women's safety in India, fueling fear, protests and demands for action.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Lawyer of Junaid Hafeez, a Pakistai scholar imprisoned for 13 years, is hopeful for his release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec738f833b1fd8d2a5c5a937420b44296756c09e9a3650d95343aee5a0bdb032</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207--6c93b577eab6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A former Fulbright scholar, Junaid Hafeez was sentenced to death under Pakistan's controversial blasphemy laws. His family and lawyer told DW there is now hope a court will overturn the conviction.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea has recently completed two road bridges easing transport to strategic allies Russia and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32b6364eb60b241f4a1c766784daed2445f33576d15b276e8ac8ec1b69d3ac36</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-/a-79473981--09998bc65869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-china/a-79473981?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two recently opened bridges are expected to ease trade and transport between North Korea and its powerful neighbors. The new connections come as Pyongyang builds strategic ties with China and Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48601a0841cb6a0ed9185cbeccf6bcf0351c2e8e14ea6f0e8014f4319fa9e430</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
